ervation before\"), read through a past operator, or on i itself."}, {"span": "c6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region", "drv.motion.leaving_region", "drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"], "justification": "The passage from x's entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region) to its leaving (drv.motion.leaving_region); straight through or opposite the arrow is read at the leaving by drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry (\"in degrees, left positive\", from kin.yaw_rate) against the turn recognition angle."}, {"span": "c9", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal", "dev.governs", "kin.speed", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted"], "justification": "Waiting is remaining halted (drv.motion.halted: \"complete cessation from movement\", kin.speed at or below the resolution) on the approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters). The applicable official traffic-control device is the signal s facing x (dev.governs on c or i; its presence is the evidence of its official status). A complete cycle of its lights is the span between two successive rises of the same display; the rises of s's circular_red with green_arrow(d) display (dev.traffic_signal) are counted from the start of the wait, the first rise opening the first complete cycle, so two complete cycles need more rises than the literal. That the signal does not change because it malfunctions or fails to detect x is read through its outcome on the head: during the wait s never displays an indication permitting x's movement, neither circular_green nor a green_arrow in the direction of x's movement (dev.traffic_signal state). Why the head stayed as it was (a fault, a detector) is not observable."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "c3", "why": "Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of 