direction, speed and proximity all enter the prediction by their degree.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "c3", "why": "Every trimobile, a motor vehicle with a seat designed to travel on three wheels, is already a member of the motorcycle aggregate claimed on span c2 (\"every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground\"): the duty is the same whether or not the word is read.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}], "applicability": "As NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: x carries one of the five aggregates of spans c2 and c4; at the observation x leaves intersection i (drv.motion.leaving_region(x, i)); read through a past operator from that leaving, x occupied i at every observation from its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region(x, i)) to the one before the leaving, and at that entry observation x occupied a carrier c (st.travel_region, rel.occupies(x, c)) with st.lane_enters(c, i) while a traffic signal s that governs c or i (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(d), d left or right; and at the leaving the heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(x, i) with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) shows a straight-through passage (absolute value below p.turn_recognition_angle) or a turn opposite d.", "obligation": "At every observation from that entry up to the leaving (read through a past operator from the leaving observation) at which x occupies i and is moving (drv.motion.moving with p.speed_resolution): for every road user p carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian that occupies a crosswalk w recorded as marking the entrance of some carrier c2 entering i (st.entrance_of(w, c2), st.lane_enters(c2, i)), and for every road user u other than x carrying ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic that occupies i, it is not the case that x and that road user approach within p.immediate_hazard_gap (prim.closest_approach_within) with a closest-approach centre distance (prim.closest_approach_distance) below p.conflict_clearance.", "params": ["p.speed_resolution", "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "p.conflict_clearance", "p.turn_recognition_angle", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"], "narrowings": [{"span": "c2", "why": "'A person driving' is read through the machine's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "c4", "why": "'riding' is read through the machine's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "c15", "why": "'lawfully' is not read: every pedestrian in such a crosswalk and every other member of traffic inside the intersection is yielded to. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is read as a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a carrier entering the intersection; a crosswalk across the exit of a one-way leg is not read.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x (ru.motorcycle), recorded from upstream, goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left); while it moves inside i a ru.pedestrian occupies the crosswalk at the far side, marking the entrance of the opposing carrier, and prim.closest_approach_within holds over p.immediate_hazard_gap with a prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_clearance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x (ru.bicycle), recorded from upstream, goes straight through i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) with no other road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x (ru.motorcycle) enters i 