{"node_id": "NRS_484B_307_9a_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-307-9a"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "vehicular traffic", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "facing the signal", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "may enter the intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "but must yield the right-of-way", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b11", "text": "Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.", "role": "definitional"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal"], "derived": [], "justification": "dev.traffic_signal: \"a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}\" and \"several states may be displayed at once\": a steady red with a green turn arrow is a head displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(dir), dir left or right. 'The signal' is the head tied to the subject's approach in span b4. No 'not a stand-in' clause applies."}, {"span": "b3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"], "derived": [], "justification": "'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"). The law's own qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out the members that are not conveyances: pedestrians (\"a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair\", the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian, which the rule requires the subject not to carry) and ridden or herded animals, for which the ontology has no class and nothing is read. Cycles and scooters stay in, as 'other conveyances'; paragraph (b) is written as an exception for them, which confirms they are vehicular traffic here."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.intersection", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "Facing the signal is the signal governing the approach the subject entered through. dev.governs: \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection, read as control of the junction itself\"; st.lane_enters: \"the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end\". The approach carrier c (st.travel_region) is the one x occupied (rel.occupies) at the observation of its latest entry into i (drv.motion.entering_region: \"its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\"), read through a past operator, with st.lane_enters(c, i); the signal governs c or i. dev.governs is 'not a stand-in' for a position and is not used as one."}, {"span": "b5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "drv.motion.entering_region: \"Road user x enters structure region r at the observation: its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before\"; r is the st.intersection, \"the region where two roadways meet\"."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry", "drv.motion.leaving_region"], "justification": "The movement made through the