aph) shows the movement a green arrow displayed at the entry indicates: at least p.turn_recognition_angle where d is left, at most minus p.turn_recognition_angle where d is right. Where arrows of both directions were displayed, the movement either indicates complies.", "params": ["p.turn_recognition_angle", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"], "narrowings": [{"span": "b6", "why": "The movement indicated by the arrow is read as the side and the size of the heading change through the intersection, judged when the subject leaves it: a passage turning at least the turn recognition angle toward the arrow's side complies, whatever lane it exits into.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x (ru.motor_vehicle), recorded from upstream, enters intersection i from lane c that a signal s governs; s displays circular_red with green_arrow(left) at the entry; x crosses i and leaves it with a heading change since entry well inside p.turn_recognition_angle (straight through)."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same entry under circular_red with green_arrow(left); x leaves i with a heading change since entry above p.turn_recognition_angle to the left."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "s displays circular_green at x's entry into i; x crosses straight through."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "x, recorded from upstream, enters i from lane c and crosses straight through, but the source does not observe s's state at the entry.", "masked": ["dev.traffic_signal"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x is a ru.bicycle; it enters i under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and leaves straight through: paragraph (b) applies (NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 engaged), so this duty does not."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [], "gaps": []}
